{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:23648059 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:23648059 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"23648059","source":"MED","pmid":"23648059","doi":"10.1111/acel.12094","title":"Prolonged lifespan with enhanced exploratory behavior in mice overexpressing the oxidized nucleoside triphosphatase hMTH1.","authorString":"De Luca G, Ventura I, Sanghez V, Russo MT, Ajmone-Cat MA, Cacci E, Martire A, Popoli P, Falcone G, Michelini F, Crescenzi M, Degan P, Minghetti L, Bignami M, Calamandrei G.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"De Luca G","lastName":"De Luca","firstName":"Gabriele","initials":"G","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2918-0124"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Environment and Primary Prevention, Istituto Superiore di Sanità, Viale Regina Elena 299, 00161 Rome, Italy."}]}},{"fullName":"Ventura I","lastName":"Ventura","firstName":"Ilenia","initials":"I"},{"fullName":"Sanghez V","lastName":"Sanghez","firstName":"Valentina","initials":"V","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4131-7480"}},{"fullName":"Russo MT","lastName":"Russo","firstName":"Maria Teresa","initials":"MT","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9545-3787"}},{"fullName":"Ajmone-Cat MA","lastName":"Ajmone-Cat","firstName":"Maria Antonietta","initials":"MA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7003-0972"}},{"fullName":"Cacci E","lastName":"Cacci","firstName":"Emanuele","initials":"E"},{"fullName":"Martire A","lastName":"Martire","firstName":"Alberto","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0538-4704"}},{"fullName":"Popoli P","lastName":"Popoli","firstName":"Patrizia","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Falcone G","lastName":"Falcone","firstName":"Germana","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Michelini F","lastName":"Michelini","firstName":"Flavia","initials":"F","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3727-4887"}},{"fullName":"Crescenzi M","lastName":"Crescenzi","firstName":"Marco","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0156-1494"}},{"fullName":"Degan P","lastName":"Degan","firstName":"Paolo","initials":"P","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0855-8896"}},{"fullName":"Minghetti L","lastName":"Minghetti","firstName":"Luisa","initials":"L","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7065-4689"}},{"fullName":"Bignami M","lastName":"Bignami","firstName":"Margherita","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Calamandrei G","lastName":"Calamandrei","firstName":"Gemma","initials":"G","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3762-3132"}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3727-4887"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4131-7480"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7003-0972"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7065-4689"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9545-3787"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0156-1494"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0538-4704"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0855-8896"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2918-0124"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3762-3132"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","related_data","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"4","volume":"12","journalIssueId":2057950,"dateOfPublication":"2013 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2013,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Aging Cell","title":"Aging cell","essn":"1474-9726","issn":"1474-9718","isoabbreviation":"Aging Cell","nlmid":"101130839"},"printPublicationDate":"2013-08-01"},"pubYear":"2013","pageInfo":"695-705","abstractText":"The contribution that oxidative damage to DNA and/or RNA makes to the aging process remains undefined. In this study, we used the hMTH1-Tg mouse model to investigate how oxidative damage to nucleic acids affects aging. hMTH1-Tg mice express high levels of the hMTH1 hydrolase that degrades 8-oxodGTP and 8-oxoGTP and excludes 8-oxoguanine from both DNA and RNA. Compared to wild-type animals, hMTH1-overexpressing mice have significantly lower steady-state levels of 8-oxoguanine in both nuclear and mitochondrial DNA of several organs, including the brain. hMTH1 overexpression prevents the age-dependent accumulation of DNA 8-oxoguanine that occurs in wild-type mice. These lower levels of oxidized guanines are associated with increased longevity and hMTH1-Tg animals live significantly longer than their wild-type littermates. Neither lipid oxidation nor overall antioxidant status is significantly affected by hMTH1 overexpression. At the cellular level, neurospheres derived from adult hMTH1-Tg neural progenitor cells display increased proliferative capacity and primary fibroblasts from hMTH1-Tg embryos do not undergo overt senescence in vitro. The significantly lower levels of oxidized DNA/RNA in transgenic animals are associated with behavioral changes. These mice show reduced anxiety and enhanced investigation of environmental and social cues. Longevity conferred by overexpression of a single nucleotide hydrolase in hMTH1-Tg animals is an example of lifespan extension associated with healthy aging. It provides a link between aging and oxidative damage to nucleic acids.","affiliation":"Department of Environment and Primary Prevention, Istituto Superiore di Sanità, Viale Regina Elena 299, 00161 Rome, Italy.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Telethon","acronym":"TI_","grantId":"GGP06100","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cells, Cultured"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Nucleus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTop